# The classic content's sound and model names, mapped to Shooter's Edge's own (sounds.tsv, models.tsv).
# Read by the map cloner and the game: `sound <classic path> <our name>`, `model <classic path> <our name>`,
# and `set <classname> <key>=<value> <field> <our name>` for the numbered sound sets a map picks by a
# number (doors, buttons, lifts, trains, triggers) or by worldspawn's worldtype (locks and keys).
# Our names are paths under sounds/ and models/ without the extension. A comment is a '#' at line start
# or after whitespace; a trailing `# pin` marks a line tools never rewrite. Edit with the free-assets skill.

